    guide: "风格内核：An explainer told only with circles, squares, triangles, arcs and straight lines, set in opaque colour on a light, matte paper. Every shape is a quantity drawn to scale (area is the amount), the shapes are the characters, and type only names them. A thin construction grid lays out each scene before anything lands, and folds away when it is done.\n\n关键特征：\n- Not Swiss Motion Graphics (there type is the material; here type is a label and the shapes carry the meaning), not Mid-century Cartoon (no characters, no faces), not Data Storytelling (no axes, ticks and legends as chrome: a ruler appears only when it measures something), not a slide deck (no header…\n- Shapes are amounts. A disc that doubles doubles its area (radius × √2); a weight three times heavier is a square of three times the area…\n- Shapes have roles. Circle = what grows or moves; square = what stays or weighs; triangle = slope, time, pivot.…\n- Point → line → plane. The protagonist starts as a dot, draws a line by moving (its path stays on screen), and becomes a plane (a field, a disc that ru…\n- The grid is visible. Construction lines draw first, shapes and letters land on them, then the lines retract.…\n\n构图与节奏：\n- Canvas 2D, flat fills, hard edges. No gradients, shadows, glows, transparency between shapes, outlines on filled shapes or rounded rectangles.\n- No pure black, no dark ground. Ink is a deep blue-black used only for line and type.\n- Reversed type on a field uses the paper colour, so protagonist and field must be dark enough to carry it.\n\n质感与动作：\n- Build on a locked frame; push in slowly once a composition is complete.\n- Move the whole group, not the camera, when the meaning changes: a slope swings flat about its corner and becomes a ruler.\n- A dark ground or large dark areas: the style turns heavy; ink is for line and type only.",
